# Architecture governance

> Full diagrams and feature map: [docs/ARCHITECTURE.md](../docs/ARCHITECTURE.md)

## Style

**Feature modules** under `src/features/<name>/`, each with up to three layers:

| Layer | Responsibility | May import |
| ----- | -------------- | ---------- |
| **presentation** | Page objects, locators, UI actions | Same-feature `state`, `@opencart-auto/pw-core` |
| **state** | Test data, path constants, env config | `src/shared` routes/types |
| **services** | HTTP calls, API assertion helpers | `src/shared`, same-feature `state` |

Public API per feature: `src/features/<name>/index.ts` only.

## Features

| Module | Domains |
| ------ | ------- |
| `home` | HomePage, Header, Footer |
| `catalog` | products, search API, ProductListingPage, Ribbon |
| `cart` | cart API, CartPage |
| `auth` | credentials, LoginPage, LogoutPage |
| `checkout` | billing data, checkout flow pages |
| `wishlist` | WishListPage |

## Shared and core

- **`src/shared/`** — `openCartRoutes`, HTTP types (no UI, no test data)
- **`packages/pw-core/`** — BasePage, BaseComponent, Wait, Soft/Hard assertions, `IProduct`, `IBillingDetails`

## Forbidden patterns

- Presentation importing `services` or another feature's internals
- Presentation importing test data from another feature's `state`
- HTTP/route logic inside page objects (use feature `services` or `state` paths)
- Static Playwright `expect` helpers inside service transport code (use `*Assertions.ts` in services layer)
- Cross-feature imports except via feature `index.ts` from tests/fixtures

## Tests

| Layer | Location | Fixture |
| ----- | -------- | ------- |
| functional / integration / e2e / hybrid | `src/tests/...` | `POMFixture` |
| api | `src/tests/api/` | `@playwright/test` `{ request }` |
| hybrid (session) | `src/tests/hybrid/` | `POMFixture` + `page.request` |
| unit (pure helpers) | `src/unit/<feature>/` | Vitest (`npm run test:unit`) |

## Architectural decisions

Non-trivial decisions require an ADR in [docs/adr/](../docs/adr/).
